<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'

import CallQueue from './lib/CallQueue.abide'
import callQueue from './lib/CallQueue.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import LeadBatch from './lib/LeadBatch.abide'
import leadBatch from './lib/LeadBatch.abide' with { type: 'text' }
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/components/combobox',
        '/helpers/hotkeys',
        '/abide-files/control-flow',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/listbox.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('the active key stays on its option while the list changes",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/listbox.test.ts',
            from: ["test('the arrows go round the ends unless `wrap` is off"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/listbox.test.ts',
            from: ["test('Enter picks and Escape calls `onescape`"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/listbox.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a click selects one, `mod` toggles, and Shift selects the run from the anchor",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/listbox.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('Space toggles, Shift with an arrow extends, and `mod+a` selects all",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/listbox.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('selecting one, the selection is the key last moved to, and a click picks it",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Walk a call queue of leads with the arrow keys">
        <p>Hand <code>listbox</code> the options — a list, or a function reading one live — and the key each is told apart by,
            and give the focused element its <code>keydown</code>. The arrows step, Home and End
            jump, and Enter calls <code>onpick</code>.</p>
        <Example code={callQueue}><CallQueue /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Mark the active lead, and call one on a click">
        <p>Spread <code>listbox</code> on the list and <code>option(key)</code> on each option:
            the option carries its id, its role, <code>aria-selected</code> and
            <code>data-active</code>, a pointer resting on it makes it active, and a click calls
            <code>onpick</code> with it. <code>idOf(key)</code> and <code>active</code> stay for
            markup of your own.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            {#for deal of leads by deal.id}
                <li {...queue.option(deal.id)}>{deal.name}</li>
            {/for}
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Hand several leads over at once">
        <p><code>multiple</code> selects many, and <code>selected</code> holds their keys. A click
            selects one lead, ⌘ or Ctrl with it adds or takes one out, and Shift takes the run from
            the last one picked. Space, Shift with an arrow and ⌘A or Ctrl+A do the same from the
            keys.</p>
        <Example code={leadBatch}><LeadBatch /></Example>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Keep the place in a list that keeps changing">
        <p>The active option is a key, so it stays on its lead while the list changes around it. Once
            the list no longer holds it, the first option is active.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="shared" code={`
            import { listbox, reactive } from '@abide/abide'

            const leads = reactive([ada, grace, linus])
            const queue = listbox({ id: 'leads', options: leads, key: (lead) => lead.id })
            queue.activate('grace')
            leads.set([ada, grace]) // grace stays active
            leads.set([ada]) // ada, the first, is active
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
